FlashInfer 0.7.0.post1: allow FP8 KV for FA2 batch MLA on SM12x

Source: MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4-Dual-DGX-Spark, glm53-flash_SM121.py,
  bake_fa2_fp8_sm12_gate(), as vendored in kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10
  image/patches/ at c748079 and retargeted there (mia_retarget.py) from
  mla/_core.py to FlashInfer 0.7's mla/_batch_mla/_backends/_fa_common.py.
License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 MiaAI-Lab (full text: ../LICENSE.MiaAI-Lab).
  FlashInfer is Apache-2.0.
Upstream: not in flashinfer v0.7.0.post1.
Purpose: the plan-time validator rejects kv_data_type=float8_e4m3fn on any
  device but SM90, although the FA2 kernel's FP8 path is portable. vLLM's
  FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90 backend on GB10 (SM121) plans FA2 with an FP8
  KV cache. The original accepts major in (9, 12) for both backends; this
  version accepts SM12x only for fa2, since fa3 is built for sm90a.
Needs: 0003 on SM12x (the FP8 tile does not fit SM12x shared memory
  without it).

--- a/flashinfer/mla/_batch_mla/_backends/_fa_common.py
+++ b/flashinfer/mla/_batch_mla/_backends/_fa_common.py
@@ -90,10 +90,12 @@
         raise ValueError(f"head_dim_kpe must be >= 0, got {head_dim_kpe}.")
     if kv_data_type == torch.float8_e4m3fn:
         major, minor = get_compute_capability(device)
-        if major != 9:
+        # The FA2 kernel's FP8 path also builds and runs on SM12x (GB10 /
+        # RTX PRO Blackwell); FA3 is still Hopper-only.
+        if major != 9 and not (major == 12 and backend == "fa2"):
             raise ValueError(
                 "FP8 kv_data_type for MLA requires an SM90 (Hopper) device, "
-                f"got SM{major}{minor}."
+                f"or an SM12x device with the fa2 backend, got SM{major}{minor}."
             )
         if q_data_type != torch.bfloat16:
             raise ValueError(
